        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ringaskiddy, County Cork, Cork, Ballincollig, Ireland\n- Organizations: National Maritime College of Ireland, Department of Defence, Cork City Council area, University College Cork, Crawford College of Art and Design\n- Topics: Education in Cork, population\n\nFacts:\n- The National Maritime College of Ireland is situated on former Department of Defence land in Ringaskiddy, County Cork.\n- The National Maritime College of Ireland opened to students in 2004.\n- In 2016, County Cork had a population of 542,196, making it the third most populous county in Ireland.\n- The Cork City Council area includes Ballincollig.\n- Cork has several third-level colleges, including University College Cork, Crawford College of Art and Design, and the National Maritime College of Ireland.",
